From 08159d49140ec70f26e8b1bd48a2d4af739ccd41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:08:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: big constant tables to constant data before
 copy_prop_vars

The BC lowmem ETC2/EAC transcoder (panvk_bc_etc2.comp) carries global
const LUTs of 1152, 512 and 128 entries. nir_lower_variable_initializers
turns each into per-element stores, and nir_opt_copy_prop_vars in
panvk_preprocess_nir() then tracks every store against every load
through all the optimization loops (nir_compare_deref_paths). That is
1.4 s to 4.3 s of CPU per transcode pipeline on a Mali-G615 phone:
PanProbe bc_decode without a shader cache went from 0.7 s (rc4) to
15.3 s.

Run nir_opt_large_constants with a 256-byte threshold before the first
copy_prop_vars, so the big tables become constant data at once. Small
tables stay for the existing pass in panvk_lower_nir(), which runs
after unrolling made their accesses direct. The pass appends to any
existing constant_data, so the second run is safe.

bc_decode on G615 v11 without cache: 15.3 s to 4.99 s, 16/16 PASS.
bc_perf warm upload GPU times unchanged within noise.
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index c1ae6aef2b4..d735f2dae26 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -748,6 +748,16 @@ panvk_preprocess_nir(struct vk_physical_device *vk_pdev,
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_global_vars_to_local);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_split_var_copies);
 
+   /* Big constant tables (the BC lowmem transcoder's EAC LUTs, 1152 + 512 +
+    * 128 entries) become constant data before the first copy_prop_vars:
+    * otherwise every one of their initializer stores is tracked against every
+    * load through all the optimization loops (nir_compare_deref_paths), 1.4 s
+    * to 4.3 s of CPU per transcode pipeline on a G615 phone. Small tables
+    * stay for panvk_lower_nir()'s pass, after unrolling made their accesses
+    * direct.
+    */
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_large_constants, NULL, 256);
+
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_copy_prop_vars);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_combine_stores, nir_var_all);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_loop);
-- 
